The training-set birefringence is identically zero for every cubic (or nearly cubic) crystal and is otherwise controlled by polarizability anisotropy. The largest values (>0.9) occur in two families: (i) the alkali-pnictide Zintl phases Cs8Sb8 / Rb8Sb8 whose orthorhombic cells contain infinite pnictogen chains, and (ii) chain- or layer-like polychalcogenides (Tl8Te12, Cs4Cu4Se16, Ba2Te6).  

Inspection of the 100 candidate POSCARs immediately eliminates all cubic entries. Among the remainder the closest structural analogues are:

- c007 (Rb8As8) – identical packing and lattice-axis ratios to the record-setting M8Pn8 phases;  
- c064 (Tl8S20) and c089 (Cs8Se12) – polychalcogenide chain structures whose metric anisotropy matches the high-dn training examples;  
- c039 (RbGeI3) – extreme 1-D cell (c/a \approx 3.75) built from polarizable iodide units;  
- c049 (RbNb4AgP2S20) – direct Rb analogue of the training compound that already reaches 0.29–0.33.

These five therefore receive the highest predicted birefringence, in the order of their similarity to the strongest training examples.

Final: c007, c064, c089, c039, c049
